      "raw": "<p>I think for the Sentinels, anything that affects &quot;A Hero&quot; or &quot;A Hero Target&quot; becomes player&#39;s choice on which Sentinel is affected.</p><p>Anything that affects multiple targets can affect more than 1 of them.&nbsp; For instance; &quot;All Hero Targets&quot; would affect all Active members of the Sentinels.&nbsp; &quot;__ damage to Hero with the highest HP and ___ damage to the Hero with the lowest HP.&quot;&nbsp; If Dr. Medico had the most out of everyone and Writhe had the least HP out of everyone, they would both take damage.</p><p>Basically, they are always treated as separate Hero targets, except for certain conditions such as Infection in Plague Rat&#39;s deck.&nbsp; The player chooses which Sentinel is actually Infected, but for the purposes of flipping Plague rat, your entire &quot;Hero Card&quot; is considered Infected (but, only the Sentinel that is actually Infected suffers the affects)</p>",
